  {t="Wild Shore: kill these as you meet them", lv=40, n="Every Bloodsail drops Snuff and one of them carries Dizzy's eye; the Swashbucklers walk the shore just north of town. The charts and orders lie in the pirate camp on the Wild Shore, south of Booty Bay.", g={{"o",604,i=2,txt="Bloodsail Charts",m=1434,x=29.6,y=80.8},{"o",587,i=1,txt="Snuff x15",m=1434,x=29.6,y=80.9},{"o",576,i=1,txt="Dizzy's Eye",m=1434,x=29.6,y=80.9},{"o",604,i=3,txt="Bloodsail Orders",m=1434,x=29.6,y=80.9},{"o",604,i=1,txt="Kill Bloodsail Swashbuckler x10",m=1434,x=31,y=81.1}}},
  {t="Booty Bay", lv=40, g={{"t",587,n2="Deeg, on the top floor",m=1434,x=26.9,y=77.3},{"a",348,m=1434,x=27.6,y=76.7,ml=40},{"t",604,m=1434,x=27.2,y=77},{"i",0,txt="Seahorn now offers The Bloodsail Buccaneers: leave it. Its three captains are level 45-48 with crews around them, and the route brings you back to Seahorn at 48 for it."},{"t",576,m=1434,x=28.6,y=75.9}}},
  {t="Gorilla hills", lv=40, n="Ride inland to the Mistvale gorilla hills. Elder Mistvale Gorillas drop the giblets; Witch Doctor Unbagwa sits among them.", g={{"o",606,i=1,txt="Mistvale Giblets x5",m=1434,x=31.1,y=67.9},{"h",2799,txt="Get Gorilla Fang x10",m=1434,x=31.1,y=67.9,n=10}}},
  {t="Unbagwa's ritual", lv=40, n="Hand in the fangs and stay: three waves of gorillas come, Mokk the Savage last. Fight at full health.", g={{"t",349,n2="Witch Doctor Unbagwa, inside Spirit Den",m=1434,x=35.3,y=60.4},{"o",348,i=1,txt="Heart of Mokk",m=1434,x=35,y=60.9}}},
  {t="Naga Explorers", lv=40, n="The naga comb the beaches north of the Bloodsail camp; they drop the reeds.", g={{"o",617,i=1,txt="Akiris Reed x10",m=1434,x=27.9,y=61.6}}},
  {t="Booty Bay", lv=40, n="Ride back down to town; Shaky stands at the tunnel mouth.", g={{"t",606,m=1434,x=26.9,y=73.6},{"a",607,m=1434,x=26.9,y=73.6,ml=30},{"t",617,m=1434,x=26.8,y=76.4},{"a",623,n2="for Privateer Groy in Theramore: keep it",m=1434,x=26.8,y=76.4,ml=38},{"a",2872,n2="for Stoley in Tanaris: keep it; on the top floor",m=1434,x=27.8,y=77.1,ml=40},{"t",348,m=1434,x=27.6,y=76.7},{"t",607,n2="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley, on the top floor",m=1434,x=27.8,y=77.1},{"a",609,m=1434,x=27.8,y=77.1,ml=30}}},
  {t="Cortello's scroll", lv=40, n="Optional: Cortello's scroll lies inside one of the three Bloodsail ships anchored off the coast just south of Booty Bay, on a middle or lower deck, and is not always on the same ship. Their crews are 42-45 pirates: clear your way from the edge, one at a time, and leave the captains (45-48), whom the route comes back for at 48.", g={{"h",4056,txt="Get Cortello's Riddle",m=1434,x=29.2,y=88.6,n=1,opt=true},{"a",624,n2="for the Swamp of Sorrows later",opt=true,ml=35}}},
  {t="Zanzil's village", lv=40, n="Every Zanzil follower can drop the mixture; Chucky \"Ten Thumbs\" walks the south of the camp.", g={{"o",621,i=1,txt="Zanzil's Mixture x12",m=1434,x=38.7,y=59.8},{"o",609,i=3,txt="Chucky's Huge Ring",m=1434,x=40,y=58.2},{"o",609,i=2,txt="Jon-Jon's Golden Spyglass",m=1434,x=34.9,y=51.8}}},
  {t="Maury and Jon-Jon", lv=40, n="Ride north to the hills west of the road. Maury \"Club Foot\" Wilkins and Jon-Jon the Crow stand together just north of Zanzil's village.", g={{"o",609,i=1,txt="Maury's Clubbed Foot",m=1434,x=35.3,y=51.3}}},
  {t="Jungle Stalkers", lv=40, n="The Jungle Stalkers roam the slopes west of the mine.", g={{"o",196,i=1,txt="Kill Jungle Stalker x10",m=1434,x=32.1,y=43.1}}},
  {t="The north-west coast", lv=40, n="Ride north-west from the mine to the bay on the north-west coast. The Giant Clams lie on its floor and hold the pearls; Gazban swims among them and drops the Stone of the Tides.", g={{"o",705,i=1,txt="Blue Pearl x9",n2="Blue Pearl; underwater",m=1434,x=26.8,y=30.8},{"o",611,i=1,txt="Stone of the Tides",m=1434,x=25,y=23.6}}},
  {t="Hemet Nesingwary", lv=40, g={{"t",196,m=1434,x=35.7,y=10.8}}},
  {t="Hemet Nesingwary", lv=40, w={{k="group",q=197}}, g={{"a",197,m=1434,x=35.7,y=10.8,ml=28}}},
  {t="Arbor Tarantula", lv=40, n="An Arbor Tarantula crawls in the jungle south-east of Nesingwary's camp, on the way to the Rebel Camp: catch one with the tool from Amaryllis Webb's Entomology Starter Kit.", w={{k="onquest",q={93176}}}, g={{"h",213566,txt="Get Arbor Tarantula Specimen",m=1434,x=43.1,y=16.7,n=1}}},
  {t="Rebel Camp", lv=40, n="Ride north-east past Nesingwary's camp and follow the road north to the camp at the top of the vale.", g={{"t",622,m=1434,x=37.7,y=3.3}}},
  {t="Brother Nimetz", lv=40, g={{"t",205,m=1434,x=37.8,y=3.6}}},
  {t="Panther Mastery", lv=40, n="These are elite mobs: grouping up is encouraged, look for people to do it with. Bhag'thera is a level 40 elite: most classes solo it at level 42, but you may need help. Skip it if you are alone: the route has you grind the XP back.", w={{k="group",q=193}}, g={{"o",193,i=1,txt="Fang of Bhag'thera",m=1434,x=49.4,y=24,grp=true}}},
  {t="Level 42.16 at Zul'Mamwe", lv=42, n="Alone, you skip Nesingwary's three elite hunts: take their experience from the Skullsplitter trolls of Zul'Mamwe instead, just east of the mine, so every kill also counts for Kebok's tusks. Or, with a group, run the Uldaman dungeon instead.", w={{k="group",neg=true,q=193},{k="group",neg=true,q=197},{k="group",neg=true,q=208},{k="level",op="<",n=42,frac=0.16}}, g={{"g",0,txt="Skullsplitter Warrior",m=1434,x=45.5,y=36.5},{"l",42,txt="Reach level 42 (16% in): grind Skullsplitter Warrior",n2="grind on Skullsplitter Warrior",m=1434,x=45.9,y=38,fr=0.16}}},
  {t="Ruins of Zul'Mamwe: kill these as you meet them", lv=42, n="The Skullsplitter trolls hold the ruins just east of the mine; any of them can drop tusks, their panthers always do.\nFollow the road north-east to the Venture Co. camp at the Crystalvein Mine; the miners, surveyors and foremen drop the crystals.\nCareful: Stealthed Shadowmaw Panthers and Stranglethorn Tigresses roam the area around the camp.", g={{"o",209,i=1,txt="Skullsplitter Tusk x18",m=1434,x=45.6,y=41.6},{"o",600,i=1,txt="Singing Blue Crystal x10",m=1434,x=42.4,y=41.4}}},
  {t="Raptor Mastery", lv=42, n="These are elite mobs: grouping up is encouraged, look for people to do it with. Tethis is a level 43 elite: most classes solo it at level 45, but you may need help. Skip it if you are alone: the route has you grind the XP back.", w={{k="group",q=197}}, g={{"o",197,i=1,txt="Talon of Tethis",m=1434,x=31.5,y=41.2,grp=true}}},
  {t="Hemet Nesingwary", lv=42, w={{k="group",q=197}}, g={{"t",197,m=1434,x=35.7,y=10.8}}},
  {t="Sir S. J. Erlgadin", lv=42, w={{k="group",q=193}}, g={{"t",193,m=1434,x=35.5,y=10.6}}},
  {t="Hemet Nesingwary", lv=42, w={{k="group",q=208}}, g={{"a",208,m=1434,x=35.7,y=10.8,ml=28}}},
  {t="Big Game Hunter", lv=42, n="These are elite mobs: grouping up is encouraged, look for people to do it with. King Bangalash is a level 43 elite: most classes solo it at level 45, but you may need help. Skip it if you are alone: the route has you grind the XP back.\nCareful: Tigers and stealthed shadowmaw panthers roam close to him. Clear them before you pull him. When he is pulled, King Bangalash calls for help from creatures within 20 yd.", w={{k="group",q=208}}, g={{"o",208,i=1,txt="Head of Bangalash",m=1434,x=38.2,y=35.6,grp=true}}},
  {t="Hemet Nesingwary", lv=42, w={{k="group",q=208}}, g={{"t",208,m=1434,x=35.7,y=10.8}}},
  {t="Level 42.16", lv=42, n="Still short of level 42.16 after the hunts you did? Make up the rest on the Cold Eye Basilisks by the Crystalvein Mine, on your way south to Booty Bay. Or, with a group, run the Uldaman dungeon instead.", w={{k="level",op="<",n=42,frac=0.16}}, g={{"g",0,txt="Cold Eye Basilisk",m=1434,x=36.3,y=42.3},{"l",42,txt="Reach level 42 (16% in): grind Cold Eye Basilisk",n2="grind on Cold Eye Basilisk",m=1434,x=36.2,y=42,fr=0.16}}},
